    "created_at": "2024-11-27T16:31:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-27T16:31:50Z",
    "body": "I don't think `xn--i29h.kz` is a good example for this topic. It contains valid punycode that decodes to the U+1FACD character. This character is `disallowed` according to `IdnaMappingTable.txt`. This means that the `ToASCII` will return a failure even if `IgnoreInvalidPunycode` is `true`.",
