    "body": "@annevk But the problem is that UTS 46 is clearly another living standard so there's no guarantee that what yesterday was invalid won't be valid tomorrow (as you noticed in https://github.com/whatwg/url/issues/836#issuecomment-2498682684), and worse even, that was valid yesterday won't be invalid tomorrow.\r\n\r\nI understand validation changing as new issues are found when it comes to displaying it to the end user for confusables protection, but parsing shall IMO remain stable when dealing with ASCII-only domains...",
